CATEGORIES:Sports Fitness
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event Organizer2026 Valkyries Free WNBA Playo
 ff Watch Party at Thrive City (SF)Valkyries fans will gather at Pier 48 fo
 r the first-ever March to Ballhalla ahead of the team’s first away game 
 of the 2026 WNBA Playoffs\, presented by Kaiser Permanente.\nThe march wil
 l begin at Pier 48 Lot A\, migrate along Terry Francois Blvd\, and end at 
 Thrive City for the Valkyries Playoffs Watch Party\, presented by Kaiser P
 ermanente. T\nhe march will feature music by the Fremont High School March
 ing Band\, city officials including San Francisco Mayor Daniel Lurie\, Val
 kyries staff\, fans\, and community organizations such as the Lowrider Cou
 ncil. Ari Waller will emcee and Valkyries Bestie Violet will be hyping up 
 marchers and meeting with fans.\n\nThe Valkyries game against the Dallas W
 ings will tip off at 6:00 p.m. following the march and will be shown in Th
 rive City.\nThis will be the second game of the First Round\, where the Va
 lkyries currently lead the Wings 1-0 in the best-of-three series.\n\nThriv
 e City hosts a Golden State Valkyries playoff watch party on September 30\
 , 2026\, preceded by the March to Ballhalla fan march. Check-in begins at 
 4:00 PM at Pier 48 Ferry Dock\, followed by a 4:30 PM march with Violet\, 
 local San Francisco lowriders\, and special guests to Thrive City. The wat
 ch party begins at 6:00 PM\, with the road game shown on the plaza board\;
  entry and seating are first come\, first served until capacity is reached
 .\nMarch to Ballhalla\n4PM — Check-In: Kick things off at Pi...\n\nFree\
 n\nTickets: https://chasecenter.com/thrive-city/\nDetails: https://sf.func
 heap.com/march-to-ballhalla-sfs-pier-48-to-thrive-city-for-valkyries-playo
