DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerAstronomy on Tap is is a free 
 public lecture series where astronomers give short\, laid-back talks over 
 drinks at local bars. No background in science required — our scientists
  share cool stuff about space while the audience sits back and relaxes\, w
 ith plenty of time to indulge their curiosity and ask whatever questions t
 hey want.\nThis month\, we’re hosting:\n\nJohn Franklin Crenshaw (Stanfo
 rd) – Before the Big Bang: Inflation and the Multiverse\nand\nSimon Stee
 l (SETI Institute) – How We (Almost) Discovered ET\nCrenshaw is a a Rubi
 n Postdoctoral Fellow at the Kavli Institute for Particle Astrophysics and
  Cosmology (KIPAC) at Stanford University. Steel is Deputy Director of the
  Carl Sagan Center for Research at the SETI Institute and Principal Invest
 igator of the NASA Community College Network.\nAstronomy on Tap takes plac
 e in cities all over the world. This is a revival of the San Francisco cha
 pter\, which regularly hosted events before the pandemic. We’re excited 
 to be back on a monthly basis!\nThe event is free\, but there is a 1 drink
  minimum. Food (tacos) will be available with vegetarian options.\nIf you
 ’d like to join our mailing list to hear about future events\, sign up h
 ere.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/astronomy-on-tap-sf-
