BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Andrea Prichett & Friends
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1634470@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerAndrea Prichett & FriendsIn an
  evening with Andrea Prichett and Friends\, you can expect to be taken on 
 something of a journey. From tender ballads to raucous political anthems\,
  the performance moves between the personal and the political and sometime
 s both at the same time.\nThe rich resonance of Andrea’s voice carries t
 he message of her original lyrics on a versatile instrumental foundation p
 rovided by Deborah Hungerford on piano and keyboards\, Mike Derrick on gui
 tar\, and Alexis Tsamoudakis on bass. The genre defying tunes range from b
 lues\, folk\, rock and even jazz at times. While Andrea’s influences inc
 lude singer-songwriters (Patti Griffin\, Tracy Chapman\, Joni Mitchell\, J
 ames Taylor\, etc)\, she also loves to dance and so the R&B/Motown sound i
 s also woven into the mix.\n\nFormerly of the Berkeley-based\, nationally-
 known feminist folk trio Rebecca Riots\, Andrea has released several album
 s. In recent times\, Andrea released a solo album\, The Frame\, and contin
 ues to write and sing about the issues of the day. A natural storyteller a
 nd political activist\, Andrea combines anecdotes with her carefully craft
 ed songs to inspire and uplift her audiences. Her fans describe the experi
 ence of going to her shows as part political\, part spiritual\, part humor
 ous and TOTALLY engaging!\nTickets are $20 in advance and $25 at the door.
  Children under 12 are free. Advance tickets are available here\, or if th
 e show is not sold out\, you may purchase your tickets at the...\n\n$20.00
 \n\nTickets: https://eventvesta.com/events/160687/t/tickets\nDetails: http
 s://sf.funcheap.com/andrea-prichett-friends/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/unname
 d-3.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:The Back Room\, 1984 Bonita Ave Berkeley\, CA 94704
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/andrea-prichett-friends/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Balkan Sundays: Duygu and Friends + Turkish Music Jam Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639884@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerJenette SellinAfter a long sum
 mer hiatus\, Balkan Sundays is back! We’ll be at Muddy Waters on 2nd Sun
 days and Ashkenaz on 4th Sundays (starting in October). This coming Balkan
  Sundays on October 11th will feature Duygu and Friends with a Turkish mus
 ic jam session that the band will lead.\nCome one come all to play some of
  your favorite Turkish repertoire. The first half of the evening will feat
 ure Duygu and Friends\, then the 2nd half will be opened up as a jam sessi
 on. As always\, it’s free. All we ask is that you support the venue by b
 uying some of their delicious food and beverages and it’s always suggest
 ed to tip the band. That’s how we keep cover free events happening. See 
 you there!\n\nDuygu & Friends covers folk songs from Anatolia and the broa
 der Mediterranean\, spanning multiple languages and musical traditions. Jo
 ining Duygu Gün on guitar and vocals are Peter Bonos on oud and trumpet\,
  Evin Sellin on violin\, Zina Pozen on accordion\, and Aaron Goldstein on 
 percussion.\nFind them on IG: duybeni\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.inst
 agram.com/balkansundays/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/balkan-sundays-
 duygu-friends-turkish-music-jam-session/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Copy-o
 f-Square-BS-1112.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Muddy Waters\, 521 Valencia Street\, San Francisco\, CA 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
