DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerBota Tapas & Paella BarBota Ta
 pas & Paella Bar near Downtown San Francisco and Union Square is doing “
 Tapas Tuesdays” and enjoy all of our delicious Spanish Tapas at 10% Off.
  Just mention “Tapas Tuesday” to our server before ordering to get the
  discount.\nAbout Bota Tapas and Paella Bar\n\nAs an age-old tradition dat
 ing back to the early 1800s\, Spanish travelers used “BOTA”\, or tradi
 tional sheep-skinned repositories\, to transport and share their wine. The
  Spaniards historically thrived on the values of sharing and community: tw
 o ideals that have buoyantly withstood the test of time. Tailored around t
 hese same ideals are Spain’s cuisine and the development of “tapas\,
 ” style dining – where individuals share small plates and memories. Fr
 om Seville to San Francisco\, and across the world\, our goal is to initia
 te more memories – this is why and how we operate. Whether it be with yo
 ur friends or family\, we here at Bota sincerely hope that you enjoy this 
 stop on your journey.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.botasf.com/\nDetails
 : https://sf.funcheap.com/tapas-tuesday-10-spanish-tapas/\nSource: Funchea
 p SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Pulpo.
 webp
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Bota Tapas & Paella Bar\, 490 Geary Street\, San Francisco\, CA 9
 4102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/tapas-tuesday-10-spanish-tapas/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Swimming Home — Documentary World Premiere + Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:dothebay-17900448@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:A feature documentary about one man's solo swim across the Eng
 lish Channel — and the promise to his mother that drove it.\n\n100% of t
 icket sales go to cancer research at Gustave Roussy\, Europe's leading can
 cer research and treatment centre\, in France.\n\nSwimming Home is a featu
 re documentary about one man's attempt to swim the English Channel — sol
 o\, without a wetsuit\, across 21 miles of cold\, unpredictable water know
 n as the "Everest of swims."\n\nThe film follows Erwan Le Roy\, a French-b
 orn San Franciscan with no endurance-swimming background\, over the year h
 e spends transforming himself\, body and mind\, for a crossing most people
  would never attempt. What starts as a promise to his mother after her can
 cer diagnosis becomes a true story about grief\, hope\, and what it takes 
 to keep going when every reason to quit is right there in the water.\n\nWo
 rld Premiere\, followed by a live Q&A with Erwan Le Roy\, the swimmer at t
 he center of the film.\nDocumentary · 74 minutes. Doors 5:00pm — screen
 ing begins promptly at 5:30pm — Q&A to follow. Event ends 7:30pm.\n\n$23
 .18\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbr
