 e your story about growing up and raising your family in San Francisco.\n\
 nEvery family has a story. Every voice matters. Please share yours.\nJoin 
 us for the District 1 Richmond Family Summit! The This Is Your City: Famil
 y Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and communi
 ty members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our city.
 \n\nThursday\, Oct. 22\, 2026\, 5:00 p.m. – 7:30 p.m.\nRichmond Recreati
 on Center\, 251 18th Ave\, San Francisco\, CA 94121\n\nFree food\, childca
 re\, and interpretation are provided. Please note all interpretation reque
 sts must be made 48 hours or more prior to the Family Summit.\nWho should 
 attend? Everyone is welcome. This event highlights District 1\, but you ca
 n attend any Family Summit that fits your schedule.\nWhy are we gathering?
  The Family Summit Series is part of San Francisco’s first Citywide Comm
 unity Needs Assessment. Through conversations with families across the cit
 y\, we’re learning what matters most to children\, youth\, young adults\
 , and families. What we learn will help improve future planning\, programs
 \, and services.\nWhether you’ve lived in San Francisco your whole life 
 or recently made it your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\nDistri
 ct 1 Neighborhoods include: Inner Richmond\, Central Richmond\, Outer Rich
 mond\, Vista del Mar\, Seacliff\, Lake District\, Presidio Terrace\, Lone 
