DESCRIPTION:Steve DisenhofPhotojournalists on the Front Lines of Protest: 
 A panel discussion hosted by Indivisible San Francisco and Pro Bono Photo.
 \nIndivisible SF presents a panel of local photojournalists from Pro Bono 
 Photo and other news organizations who will share selections from their po
 rtfolios and discuss the role photojournalism plays in documenting protest
 \, civic action and pro-democracy movements.\nFrom the civil rights and vo
 ting rights movements of the 1960s to today’s social justice actions\, t
 he San Francisco Bay Area has long been a significant site of protest and 
 civil disobedience. Who documents these fleeting moments of protest and ci
 vic action? Local photojournalists share their experiences covering pro-de
 mocracy movements and street demonstrations throughout the Bay Area.\n\nHe
 ar firsthand accounts from photographers documenting recent protests and d
 emonstrations\, view a curated projection of their work and engage directl
 y with the panelists during an audience Q&A.\nPop-Up Gallery: A selection 
 of photographs by participating photojournalists will be displayed alongsi
 de historical protest photography from SFPL collections\, connecting conte
 mporary documentation of Bay Area demonstrations with the Library’s phot
 ographic record of protest and civic action. The display will be on view o
 n the 4th Floor of the Main Library from Sept. 17–Dec. 31.\nModerator\nJ
 ack Owicki\, founder of Pro Bono Photo\, founded the organization after co
 ordinating photography for the Bay Area Women’s Mar...\n\nFree\n\nTicket
 s: https://on.sfpl.org/10-22-26\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/free-pan
 el-bay-area-protest-photojournalists-popup-exhibit-sf-main-library/\nSourc
 e: Funcheap SF
