DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Department of Children\, Youth & Their Families 
 (DCYF)\n\nThis is Your City. This is Your Voice. This is Your Future. Shar
 e your story about growing up and raising your family in San Francisco.\n\
 nEvery family has a story. Every voice matters. Please share yours.\nJoin 
 us for the District 11 Excelsior Family Summit! The This Is Your City: Fam
 ily Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and commu
 nity members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our cit
 y.\n\nThursday\, Oct. 29\, 2026\, 5:30 p.m. – 8:00 p.m.\nIslais Place\, 
 4840 Mission St. SF\, CA 94112\n\nFree food\, childcare\, and interpretati
 on are provided. Please note all interpretation requests must be made 48 h
 ours or more prior to the Family Summit.\nWho should attend? Everyone is w
 elcome. This event highlights District 11\, but you can attend any Family 
 Summit that fits your schedule.\nWhy are we gathering? The Family Summit S
 eries is part of San Francisco’s first Citywide Community Needs Assessme
 nt. Through conversations with families across the city\, we’re learning
  what matters most to children\, youth\, young adults\, and families. What
  we learn will help improve future planning\, programs\, and services.\nWh
 ether you’ve lived in San Francisco your whole life or recently made it 
 your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\nDistrict 11 Neighborhoods 
 include: Excelsior\, Crocker Amazon\, Outer Mission\, Mission Terrace\, Oc
 eanview\, Ingleside\, Ingleside Heights\, Merced Heights\n\nFree\n\nTicket
 s: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/district-11-excelsior-family-summit-ticket
 s-1996547093101?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/distri
 ct-11-excelsior-family-summit/\nSource: Funcheap SF
