DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Department of Children\, Youth & Their Families 
 (DCYF)\n\nThis is Your City. This is Your Voice. This is Your Future. Shar
 e your story about growing up and raising your family in San Francisco.\n\
 nEvery family has a story. Every voice matters. Please share yours.\nJoin 
 us for the District 2 Marina Family Summit! The This Is Your City: Family 
 Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and community
  members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our city.\n
 \nSaturday\, Nov. 7\, 2026\, 11:00 a.m. – 1:30 p.m.\nMarina Middle Schoo
 l\, 3500 Fillmore St\, SF\, CA 94123\n\nFree food\, childcare\, and interp
 retation are provided. Please note all interpretation requests must be mad
 e 48 hours or more prior to the Family Summit.\nWho should attend? Everyon
 e is welcome. This event highlights District 2\, but you can attend any Fa
 mily Summit that fits your schedule.\nWhy are we gathering? The Family Sum
 mit Series is part of San Francisco’s first Citywide Community Needs Ass
 essment. Through conversations with families across the city\, we’re lea
 rning what matters most to children\, youth\, young adults\, and families.
  What we learn will help improve future planning\, programs\, and services
 .\nWhether you’ve lived in San Francisco your whole life or recently mad
 e it your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\nDistrict 2 Neighborho
 ods include: Marina\, Cow Hollow\, Pacific Heights\, Presidio Heights\, Jo
 rdan Park\, Laurel Heights\, Presidio\, Lower Pacific Heights\, Cathedral 
 Hill\, an...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/district-2-m
 arina-family-summit-tickets-1996548210443?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDetails: http
