DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Department of Children\, Youth & Their Families 
 (DCYF)\n\nThis is Your City. This is Your Voice. This is Your Future. Shar
 e your story about growing up and raising your family in San Francisco.\n\
 nEvery family has a story. Every voice matters. Please share yours.\nJoin 
 us for the District 4 Sunset Family Summit! The This Is Your City: Family 
 Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and community
  members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our city.\n
 \nSaturday\, Nov. 14\, 2026\, 11:00 a.m. – 1:30 p.m.\nSunset Recreation 
 Center\, 2201 Lawton St\, SF\, CA 94122\n\nFree food\, childcare\, and int
 erpretation are provided. Please note all interpretation requests must be 
 made 48 hours or more prior to the Family Summit.\nWho should attend? Ever
 yone is welcome. This event highlights District 4\, but you can attend any
  Family Summit that fits your schedule.\nWhy are we gathering? The Family 
 Summit Series is part of San Francisco’s first Citywide Community Needs 
 Assessment. Through conversations with families across the city\, we’re 
 learning what matters most to children\, youth\, young adults\, and famili
 es. What we learn will help improve future planning\, programs\, and servi
 ces.\nWhether you’ve lived in San Francisco your whole life or recently 
 made it your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\nDistrict 4 Neighbo
 rhoods include: Central Sunset\, Outer Sunset\, Parkside\, Pine Lake Park\
 , Lakeshore\, Merced Manor\, and Farallon Islands\n\nFree\n\nTickets: http
 s://www.eventbrite.com/e/district-4-sunset-family-summit-tickets-199654922
 6482?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/district-4-sunset
 -family-summit/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/12_D4_
